      "content": "### Bellamkonda Restaurants Ltd. (textbook example, p. 259)\n\n| Statement of financial position, as at 31st October 20XX | $'000 | $'000 |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| **Noncurrent assets** | | |\n| Property, plant & equipment | 1,700 | |\n| Machinery and equipment | 500 | |\n| | | 2,200 |\n| Accumulated depreciation | | (200) |\n| **Noncurrent assets** | | **2,000** |\n| **Current assets** | | |\n| Cash | 250 | |\n| Debtors | 30 | |\n| Stocks | 200 | |\n| **Current assets** | | **480** |\n| **Total assets** | | **2,480** |\n| **Current liabilities** | | |\n| Bank overdraft | 15 | |\n| Trade creditors | 250 | |\n| Other short-term loans | 55 | |\n| **Current liabilities** | | **320** |\n| **Noncurrent liabilities** | | |\n| Borrowings (long term) | 500 | |\n| **Noncurrent liabilities** | | **500** |\n| **Total liabilities** | | **820** |\n| **Net assets** | | **1,660** |\n| **Equity** | | |\n| Share capital | 1,000 | |\n| Retained earnings | 660 | |\n| **Total equity** | | **1,660** |\n\nKey terms from the example: **accumulated depreciation** is the provision for the fall in value of noncurrent assets over time (e.g. wear and tear of restaurant equipment); **total assets** = noncurrent + current assets; **total liabilities** = noncurrent + current liabilities; **net assets** must match equity.\n\n### IB Format: Table 17.3 (profit-making business entity)\n\n| Statement of financial position for (Company Name) as at (Date) | $m | $m |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Property, plant and equipment | 500 | |\n| Accumulated depreciation | (20) | |\n| **Total noncurrent assets** | | **480** |\n| Cash | 10 | |\n| Debtors | 12 | |\n| Stocks | 35 | |\n| **Total current assets** | | **57** |\n| **Total assets** | | **537** |\n| Bank overdraft | 5 | |\n| Trade creditors | 15 | |\n| Other short-term loans | 22 | |\n| **Total current liabilities** | | **42** |\n| Borrowings (long term) | 300 | |\n| **Total noncurrent liabilities** | | **300** |\n| **Total liabilities** | | **342** |\n| **Net assets** | | **195** |\n| Share capital* | 110 | |\n| Accumulated retained profit | 85 | |\n| **Total equity** | | **195** |\n\n*Sole traders, partnerships and non-profit entities record no share capital. (Note: the printed textbook table shows total assets as 342; the correct sum of 480 + 57 is **537**, which is what makes net assets of 195 balance with equity.)\n\n### Worked Solution: Question 17.5 Marc Brothers Motor Repairs (calculated from the textbook data), as at 31st March\n\n| Item | $ | $ |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Property | 630,000 | |\n| Machinery and vehicles | 230,000 | |\n| Accumulated depreciation | (144,000) | |\n| **Total noncurrent assets** | | **716,000** |\n| Cash | 12,000 | |\n| Debtors | 16,000 | |\n| Stock | 30,000 | |\n| **Total current assets** | | **58,000** |\n| **Total assets** | | **774,000** |\n| Overdraft | 13,000 | |\n| **Total current liabilities** | | **13,000** |\n| Long-term bank loan | 380,000 | |\n| **Total noncurrent liabilities** | | **380,000** |\n| **Total liabilities** | | **393,000** |\n| **Net assets** | | **381,000** |\n| Share capital | 300,000 | |\n| Retained earnings | 81,000 | |\n| **Total equity** | | **381,000** |\n\n### Worked Solution: Question 17.7 Senjaya Fabrics Ltd (calculated from the textbook data; IDR m, as at 31st March)\n\n| Item | IDR m | IDR m |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Property | | 350 |\n| Cash 32, Debtors 35, Stocks 60 | | 127 |\n| **Total assets** | | **477** |\n| Overdraft 30, Trade creditors 45 | | 75 |\n| Mortgage (noncurrent) | | 127 |\n| **Total liabilities** | | **202** |\n| **Net assets** | | **275** |\n| Share capital 175 + Retained earnings 100 | | **275** |",
