      "content": "| Limitation | Explanation |\n|---|---|\n| **Single year in isolation** | Of little value; a **series** of final accounts is needed to identify **trends** |\n| **Human resources ignored** | Skills, loyalty, goodwill and motivation of employees are overlooked, yet failure to retain or motivate staff can seriously affect future finances |\n| **Non-financial matters ignored** | Nothing about **organizational culture** or contributions to **local communities**; qualitative factors matter (e.g. ethical objectives, location of industry) |\n| **Benchmarking is time-consuming** | Access to other businesses' accounts is needed to compare with competitors |\n| **Not the whole truth** | Firms limit, within reason, what they disclose because accounts are **public** and accessible to **competitors** |\n| **Historical** | Past performance is not necessarily indicative of current or future performance |\n\nTOK: Thomas Carlyle said \"You may prove anything by figures\".",
